400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (Overfitting and underfitting are two ends of the bias-variance trade-off. A model with high bias is too simple \(underfits\), while a model with high variance is too sensitive to the training data \(overfits\). The aim is to find the right complexity so that total error on unseen data is minimum. Other challenges include lack of interpretability of complex models, bias and fairness, privacy and security, concept drift after deployment, and shortage of skilled people. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
